        "nobel_worthiness": "GLP-1 physiology led to a major therapeutic class that has transformed treatment of diabetes and obesity while illuminating enteroendocrine control of metabolism.",
        "attribution": "Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker provide a defensible chain from identification and characterization of the hormone to its physiological and therapeutic development.",
        "maturity": "Clinical benefit and broad implementation are firmly established, with extensive evidence across metabolic disease.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Translating GLP-1 biology into medicines involved substantial additional medicinal-chemistry and industrial contributions.",
          "The most appropriate balance between foundational physiology and therapeutic development is contestable."
