      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Long-term potentiation supplied a durable cellular framework for activity-dependent synaptic change and has deeply influenced neuroscience of learning and memory.",
        "attribution": "Lømo and Bliss are central to the original phenomenon, while Morris made important links between synaptic plasticity and memory; the allocation is defensible though incomplete.",
        "maturity": "The phenomenon is robust across experimental preparations and has supported decades of mechanistic and behavioral research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Whether LTP alone constitutes the synaptic basis of memory is an oversimplification.",
          "The listed field includes more major contributors than the three-person limit permits."
